# Frame and overlays: Rotate turns a positioned box when it is painted, around its center or around Rotate origin.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Frame and overlays · Rotate and Rotate origin
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: stage
			Box:
				Height: 110
		For style: stamp
			Box:
				Padding: 4 10
				Border: 1.5
				Border color: #A32D2D
			Typography:
				Color: #A32D2D
				Bold: true
				Size: 11
		For style: pin
			Box:
				Width: 6
				Height: 6
				Corner radius: 50%
				Background: #A32D2D
	Section:
		Text: Frame and overlays
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Rotate and Rotate origin
		Paragraph: A rotated `Frame`, `Overlay` or `Page overlay` keeps its place in the layout and is turned when painted, clockwise in degrees. `Rotate origin` is the point it turns around: keywords such as `top left`, or two measures from its top left corner. The red dot marks the corner of the box before the turn.
			Style: intro
		Text: Rotate: 12  (around the center, by default)
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Style: stage
			Overlay:
				Offset: 40 auto auto 60
				Rotate: 12
				Text: DRAFT
					Style: stamp
		Text: Rotate: 30, Rotate origin: top left
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Style: stage
			Overlay:
				Offset: 47 auto auto 57
				Block:
					Style: pin
			Overlay:
				Offset: 50 auto auto 60
				Rotate: 30
				Rotate origin: top left
				Text: APPROVED
					Style: stamp
		Text: Rotate: -90, Rotate origin: top left  (vertical text along the left edge)
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Style: stage
			Overlay:
				Offset: 100 auto auto 10
				Rotate: -90
				Rotate origin: top left
				Text: VERTICAL
					Style: stamp
		Text: Rotate: 45 on a Frame with Rotate origin: 20 50%
			Style: label
		Block:
			Box:
				Height: 100
			Frame:
				Offset: 30 auto auto 80
				Rotate: 45
				Rotate origin: 20 50%
				Box:
					Width: 140
				Text: A rotated Frame
					Style: stamp
